cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Raw vs LOESS vs SERRF normalization comparison for untargeted LC-MS data"
abstract: >-
  R workflow comparing uncorrected, LOESS-corrected and SERRF-corrected
  untargeted LC-MS peak areas (Compound Discoverer 3.4 exports) across analytical
  batches, with PQC-anchored between-batch scaling, CV assessment of quality-control
  materials, and PCA coloured by batch.
authors:
  - family-names: "Piskláková"
    given-names: "Barbora"
    affiliation: "Section for Metabolomics & Lipidomics, Oslo University Hospital"
  - family-names: "Kvasnička"
    given-names: "Aleš"
    affiliation: "Section for Metabolomics & Lipidomics, Oslo University Hospital"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - metabolomics
  - lipidomics
  - LC-MS
  - batch correction
  - LOESS
  - SERRF
